      "relevant_relationships": [],
      "concrete_prior_utterances": [
        {
          "id": "msg-0001",
          "text": "Box 14B finally gave me something better than mildew. A 1986 maintenance manual for Pump Station 4 has a pencil note across section 4: ‘Ignore this in rain. Valve sticks.’ There is a brown tide mark through the sentence. The archive label says the station closed in 2009. The parts inventory says the same valve model was still on a city shelf in 2018. Rhea, is this a manual or a hostage note?"
        },
        {
          "id": "msg-0008",
          "text": "Found it. Two requests for a $43.20 valve gasket, both stamped DEFER—NEXT QUARTER. Three weeks after the second denial, the rain note appears in a different hand. I cannot prove the note was a workaround. I can prove somebody had excellent timing."
        }
